Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kompakt: fast speed is the count asked for

kompakt_wf_a2frames took 2 to 9, shortened only for 7 and below and
lengthened only for 8 and 9. The panel reports about 8 C in a 20 C room,
so at Mudita's +11 offset the A2 band has 11 frames, not 7: 8 and 9 did
nothing there, and "7" was 11.

It now takes 2 to 11 and gives every band exactly that count; 0 still
leaves the band's own. The Kompakt app's Fast mode speed row (11, 9, 8,
7, 6, 5) writes the count, and 0 when both speed rows are Mudita's.
---
--- a/drivers/misc/mudita/eink_loader/loader.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mudita/eink_loader/loader.c
@@ -1380,9 +1380,9 @@
     if (group != WF_A2)
         return 0;
 
-    /* Kompakt: up to 7 any count below the band's own; 8 and 9 (Caster's) only lengthen. a2short is 5. */
+    /* Kompakt: the count asked for, 2 to 11, whatever the band's own; 0 leaves the band alone. a2short is 5. */
     w = WF_A2N(flags);
-    if (w > WF_A2_STOCK_N ? w > n : w && w < n) {
+    if (w && w != n) {
         nn = w;
         done |= WF_A2SHORT;
     }
@@ -1787,7 +1787,7 @@
 static ssize_t kompakt_wf_a2frames_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
                                          const char *buf, size_t count)
 {
-    return wf_store_val(buf, count, WF_A2N_SHIFT, WF_A2N_MASK, 2, 9);
+    return wf_store_val(buf, count, WF_A2N_SHIFT, WF_A2N_MASK, 2, 11);
 }
 static ssize_t kompakt_wf_gl16trim_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr, char *buf)
 {
